<title>ROMANIA: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>ROMANIA GOVERNMENT LIST (961211)</p>
<p>President (Sworn in 29 Nov 96 for a four-year</p>
<p>     term..................................Emil CONSTANTINESCU</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>COALITION GOVERNMENT (To be sworn in 12 Dec 96)</p>
<p>(NOTE: The governing coalition includes the Democratic</p>
<p>	   Convention (CDR) bloc, the Social Democratic Union</p>
<p>	   (USD) and the Hungarian Democratic Union (UDMR))</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Prime Minister........................Victor CIORBEA (PNT-CD)</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS OF STATE:</p>
<p> Finance...............................Mircea CIUMARA (PNT-CD)</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs...........................Adrian SEVERIN (PD)</p>
<p> Industry &amp; Trade................Calin POPESCU-TARICEANU (PNL)</p>
<p> Reform..................................Ulm SPINEANU (PNT-CD)</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Agriculture &amp; Food Industry..........Dinu GAVRILESCU (PNT-CD)</p>
<p> Communications.............................Sorin PANTIS (PNL)</p>
<p> Culture...................................Ion CARAMITRU (PAR)</p>
<p> Defence....................................Victor BABIUC (PD)</p>
<p> Education............................Virgil PETRESCU (PNT-CD)</p>
<p> Environment, Forestry &amp; Water.................Ion OLTEAN (PD)</p>
<p> Health.......................Stefan Iosif DRAGULESCU (PNT-CD)</p>
<p> Interior................................Gavril DEJEU (PNT-CD)</p>
<p> Justice..................................Valeriu STOICA (PNL)</p>
<p> Labour &amp; Social Security...........Alexandru ATHANASIU (PSDR)</p>
<p>Parliamentary Relations...Bogdan Nicolae NICULESCU-DUVAZ (PD)</p>
<p> Public Works....................Nicolae Stefan NOICA (PNT-CD)</p>
<p> Research &amp; Technology..............Bujor Bogdan TEODORIU (PD)</p>
<p> Tourism..................................Akos BIRTALAN (UDMR)</p>
<p> Transport.................................Traian BASESCU (PD)</p>
<p> Youth &amp; Sports........................Sorin STANESCU (PNL-CD)</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>JUNIOR MINISTERS IN CHARGE OF:</p>
<p> Ethnic Minorities.........................Gyorgy TOKAY (UDMR)</p>
<p> European Integration................Alexandru HERLEA (PNT-CD)</p>
<p>General Secretariat &amp;</p>
<p>    Local Administration..................Remus OPRIS (PNT-CD)</p>
<p> Public Relations..........................Radu BOROIANU (PNL)</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>STATE SECRETARIES, MEMBERS OF THE GOVERNMENT:</p>
<p> Defence......................Constantin Dudu IONESCU (PNT-CD)</p>
<p> Finance.................................Dan Radu RUSANU (PNL)</p>
<p> Industry &amp; Trade.....................Florin BURUIANA (PNT-CD)</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>PARTY AFFILIATIONS:</p>
<p>National Peasant Party -- (PNT-CD)</p>
<p>National Liberal Party -- (PNL)</p>
<p>National Liberal Party-CD -- (PNL-CD)</p>
<p>&amp; the Romanian Alternative Party (PAR) are part of the CDR</p>
<p>									   bloc.</p>
<p>Democratic Party -- (PD)</p>
<p>&amp; the Social Democratic Party (PSDR) form the USD.</p>
<p>Hungarian Democratic Union -- (UDMR)</p>
<p>			   - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor..........................Mugur ISARESCU</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
